# BUGS

A pin's GPIO function is not set for a GPIO's user: k1-gpio(3) drives a pin as firmware or a state left its function.
A state's pins are set even where another state already took one; nothing tracks which device holds a pin.
Only the SD card's pads' power domain is set; the other outside-powered pins' (47 to 52, 75 to 80, 98 to 103) are left as firmware set them.
The keys allow the next protected access on the bus, not one by this driver: another between the two would take it.
